; v0.1 release suite, part 2 of 2 -- after a real reboot, then TLS.
;     Execute PAYLOAD:R/REL2
; Every command appends to RAM:rel2-console.txt itself. Measured on AROS One on 2026-09-19:
; redirecting Execute (or Run ... Execute) does not capture the output of the
; commands inside the script, while a redirection on each command does. A line
; that writes a test fixture keeps its own single redirection.

FAILAT 21
Delete RAM:rel2-console.txt QUIET
Copy PAYLOAD:APKG RAM:apkg
Copy PAYLOAD:PUTFILE RAM:putfile
Protect RAM:putfile +e
Protect RAM:apkg +e
Delete RAM:rel ALL FORCE QUIET
MakeDir RAM:rel
Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "== v0.1 release suite, part 2: after the reboot =="
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --version

Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "*N==== H. the transaction interrupted before the reboot ===="
Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "read-only view must warn, not show a settled state:"
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root SYS:PkgRel list
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root SYS:PkgRel --machine onetest --run-id h2 --expect 0 --report RAM:rel/h2.json doctor --retry
If EXISTS SYS:PkgRel/db/installed/cls.json
  Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "FAIL h: registry of an uncommitted install survived"
Else
  Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "PASS h: uncommitted install rolled back after a reboot"
EndIf
If EXISTS SYS:PkgRel/cls.info
  Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "FAIL h: icon survived"
Else
  Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "PASS h: icon rolled back after a reboot"
EndIf

Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "*N==== I. TLS, negative: every one of these must be REFUSED ===="
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root RAM:N --verify-name example.invalid --machine onetest --run-id n1 --expect 12 --report RAM:rel/n1.json update
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root RAM:N --verify-name www.google.com --machine onetest --run-id n2 --expect 12 --report RAM:rel/n2.json update
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root RAM:N --index-url http://archives.arosworld.org/share/RECENT.readme --machine onetest --run-id n3 --expect 12 --report RAM:rel/n3.json update
Rename ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.crt ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.hidden
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root RAM:N --machine onetest --run-id n4 --expect 12 --report RAM:rel/n4.json update
Rename ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.hidden ENV:SYS/Certificates/ca-bundle.crt
Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "and the positive control, so the refusals above are not just no network:"
RAM:apkg >>RAM:rel2-console.txt --root RAM:N --machine onetest --run-id n0 --expect 0 --report RAM:rel/n0.json update
Echo >>RAM:rel2-console.txt "== end of part 2 =="

; Evidence out, as the last step: nothing may be typed into this Shell while
; the script runs -- keystrokes land in its input and get spliced into output.
RAM:putfile RAM:rel2-console.txt
Join RAM:rel/#?.json AS RAM:rel2-reports.txt
RAM:putfile RAM:rel2-reports.txt
